+For finite `$p >= 1`, `pNorm($p)` scales component magnitudes before raising them to a power,
+avoiding intermediate overflow and underflow for extreme finite values. Zero vectors return zero.
+Any `NAN` component gives `NAN`, including alongside infinity; otherwise, an infinite component
+or a norm exceeding the float range gives positive infinity.
+
